This repository redistributes test material published by the protocols it verifies,
so that anyone can reproduce the results without trusting this repository:

- vectors/inam/vectors.json and vectors/inam/BRON-README.md
  from inamprotocol/inam-protocol, interop/countersigned, at commit
  d5e5f4555e7fd2ca8dedfa28bbfcddb0e6eb991d. Apache-2.0. Unmodified.
  Those files contain test keys and made-up addresses only, as their own README states.

- vectors/inam/canonical-vectors.json
  from inamprotocol/inam-protocol, interop/canonical/vectors.json, at commit
  d4a2940f936af5353a9a9bf89db1097ca91bdd3c. Apache-2.0. Unmodified.
  Key-order and escaping cases with characters beyond U+FFFF and lone surrogates.
  Their maintainer published these after the ones above and pointed us at them, since
  they are where two implementations written from the same text most easily diverge:
  they exposed a real bug in their own Python canonicalizer, which sorted keys by code
  point instead of by UTF-16 code unit.

- The worked example in src/x402-offer-receipt.mjs (asset, authorizer, nonce, salt and
  the expected commitment) is quoted from x402-foundation/x402,
  specs/extensions/extension-offer-and-receipt.md section 5.6.2, on the branch
  receipt-authorization-commitment at commit 0e492d6. Apache-2.0.

Neither project has reviewed or endorsed this repository. The verifiers here were
written against the published specifications, not against those projects' source code,
which is the point: two implementations that have not seen each other agreeing on the
same vectors is evidence, and one implementation agreeing with itself is not.
